The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This route retains all thirty final-trained physical layers, executes the
middle twenty twice, and adds only the shared mapped-input projection and
zero-initialized tanh gate before both middle passes. There is no LoRA or
encoder-intermediate injection. It supplies model-only audit, conversion and reload,
without training or optimizer state. Implementation identities and release
file hashes are recorded in the converted manifest and audit reports.
